+# Potency lens: #1053, SIM-split-a (key holders), head 54bbace
+
+Record: PR #1053 · package SIM-split · head 54bbace
+
+Scope: the PR at 54bbace. Tier A. Security is a separate record (reviews/security/2026-10-12-pr1053.md).
+
+Question: where does the change cap capability without buying matching security or UX?
+
+- Pass: holders are opt-in and all-or-nothing in `egress.Config`; with the vault configured the proxy path is unchanged (full `./egress/...` suite passes), so nothing an agent can do today is narrowed.
+- Pass: the holder serves the same adapter declarations, forwarded headers, exchange swap and inference transport pool as the proxy (`egress/holderapi.go`), so a routed model call keeps its behaviour, streaming included (`stream` flushes per read).
+
+Findings:
+- **Release**, folded into builder row 1 (production wiring): the holder's netguard carries no compute-host pins (H-7), so once wired a model call to an owner-pinned compute host or private hosted route (CAP-13) is refused (fail closed).
+- **Release**, builder row 3: `agentos-holder` refuses exchange adapters until refreshed tokens persist through the unlock step (CRED-5); a worker-held or broker-held refresh route cannot move to a holder until then.
+- **Later**, in LATER.md: the holder serves read-verb operations only; today's catalog (OpenAI, Anthropic) is read-only, but an adapter with an intent-gated write verb cannot route through a holder yet.
+
+Findings: blocker 0; release 2 (builder rows 1 and 3); later 1.
+
+Arbitration: no tension with Security or UX.
